A||||24||Leadfoot||Civic Si Spanking||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||08-09-2001||10:53 AM||||I was coming home from work last night an I noticed that a guy in a Civic, about a couple of cars behind me, kept weaving in and out of lanes in a hurry.  By the time I reached the first light from my work the guy was right beside me.  He had a red Civic Si, stickers, wing, big (loud) exhaust....in short it was thoroughly riced.  As we were sitting there at the light the guy started to tap his throttle.  So I looked over at him and the guy said "You want to try?".  I figured why not.  Now I usually don't race people because it both dangerous and risky, but I had to see how I would do.  I did a quick scan for cops and prepared for the green light.  Soon as it turned green I let go of the clutch while hammered the throttle.  My tires gave out a squeal and I was off.  By the time I hit 3rd I noticed that the civic was about 5 car lengths behind me.  I figured he's got to be faster than that so I hit the brakes to see if everything was fine (not to mention I was about to miss my turn).  As he approached me I saw that his face had a pissed off look and and that he was still going through the gears.  Is it possible that the guy spun the clutch?  I am just really surprised at the margin I was up by.  Especially when I only have a stock 2.8 with 1000 miles on it.  What would you guys say?  Is this a confirmed kill or did I just get lucky?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierokid87||08-09-2001||11:48 AM||||Id say you murdered him.  Good kill.  Hondas 0 Fieros 22  <P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||08-09-2001||01:26 PM||||He could have been spinning his tires.  My friend is coming to town from jersey with his riced out SI.  I will see what my car does aginst him and let you know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The SI Civic has a 1.6L DOHC Vtec 4 cyl with 160 hp.  Not too bad for a 4.<P><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||08-09-2001||02:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>He could have been spinning his tires.  My friend is coming to town from jersey with his riced out SI.  I will see what my car does aginst him and let you know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The SI Civic has a 1.6L DOHC Vtec 4 cyl with 160 hp.  Not too bad for a 4.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Guess they should put the wing in the front.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  The added weight might help them hook up.  Although, I don't recall hearing his tires spinning.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||08-09-2001||02:50 PM||||Certainly not trying to steal your thunder or anything ...<P>Maybe it was an EX model with the SOHC VTEC and 127 horsepower ... BADGED as an Si.<P>[edited because I forgot that the 1992-1995 Civic EX had 125 horsepower but 1996-1999 EX models got bumped to 127.]<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||11
