Z||000007||Slid||08-09-2001||05:37 PM||||It sounds like he stalled it?  What speed were you going in 3rd?  Around 60 I would imagine.<P>lol, maybe he was in reverse, I remember seeing a Porsche race (video) revving up a track then he flew backwards!  Damn those 6speeds with reverse at the top left!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||NOS3800||08-09-2001||05:47 PM||||In my opinion its a KILL! I mean, the guy asked you if you wanted to try, you obliged him and proceeded to kick his rice ass! SI's are pretty weak off the line, if you continued through to say a 1/4 mile distance he probably would have at least caught you if not passed you. The VTEC takes awhile to spool up, like a turbo. At the track SI's are running 15.7-16.5. Mostly due to the driver not knowing how to drive the car. One SI was running 15.2 but even he was surprised at that, saying all his buddies SI's were high 15's at best.<BR>If the driver spun, then tough poo! Its a race, if you can't control the tire spin then don't antagonize a race.<BR>My motto" OK, you sit there and spin, I'll be at half track before you hook up"<P><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000009||85fierogt||08-09-2001||05:59 PM||||yah buddy you wooped him, up top!<BR>good job||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fatal Error||08-09-2001||06:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B><BR>The SI Civic has a 1.6L DOHC Vtec 4 cyl with 160 hp.  Not too bad for a 4.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Correct me if I'm wrong, but the SI was not a DOHC v-tec, it was SOHC. Which put out considerably less hp .. around 127. There is another thread about someone test driving a De la Sol &lt;sp?&gt; I believe in the O/T section referring to this engine type. <P>In any case .. Good kill!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>P.S.<BR>Any "ricer" car is not a bad car, it's just the stereo type people have brought it down with. Performance is performance, if the thing actually puts out gross amounts of hp .. then those wings are cool, but for all those 2 level winged 127hp civics .. those are the ones given them the bad name. IF anything they slow them down with all the extra weight. Might as well tie a brick to the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>l8r<P>-Fatal<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroMaster88||08-09-2001||06:46 PM||||The EX Civic uses the SOHC Vtec engine which puts out 127HP.  The SI Civic has the DOHC Vtec and puts out 160HP.  I believe it is the same with the Del Sol...but some SI Del slow's had the SOHC and some had the DOHC.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||08-09-2001||06:47 PM||||No, the Civic Si has the B16A vtec, DOHC, rated at 160 but easy to get 170 or 180 with minor mods.  <P>I think it was a kill too.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||firstfiero||08-09-2001||08:12 PM||||     I just posted beating an si twice about two weeks ago. I like them alot for jap. cars. The v tech is pretty darn impresive but....in a block to block race are v6 is faster. They don't have that off the line torque like we do...That vtech doesn't kick in to like 6000 grand and by then you should already have a sizable lead. both times I dogged him by 4 to 5 car lengths. If your going ot race him for a half mile or more expect that high end torque to catch up to you. <BR>    Yes...your damn right it's a nice kill!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||b lo 0||08-10-2001||12:13 AM||||Umm, you got real lucky, or he sucks at driving.  I've seen new Si's ('99) eat Z28's alive (I was actually in the car, and it had a cold air and exhaust, that's all).  Really fast until you add a 500 lb wing-lol   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW, '99 Si's are DOHC and the Vtec comes online at 4,000 rpm, and you can feel it.  Sure, the Camaro beat us off the line, but by the 1-2 shift we were ahead.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">        <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!<p>[This message has been edited by b lo 0 (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||08-10-2001||12:24 AM||||Eat Z-28's alive??<P>perhaps an 85 Carb z28. Don't think a Si has a prayer against a 1LE , GTA , LT1 or LS1 Camaro , not without a turbo or a lot of NOS.<P><BR>JM||||reg||1
Z||000016||kempo||08-10-2001||12:34 AM||||2FastTom and myself got into a race with what appeared to be a brand new Honda Vtech, your average ricer and girlfriend.  I was in my fiero, far right lane, Tom in the far left lane, and the ricer in the center (3 lane highway).  It began at around 60mph, drop into third, and our 2 fiero's royally killed the riced out vtech.  He couldn't keep up.  So we know that they aren't that great with top end, as by the time we hit 80, we were both about even, and left the ricer about 4 car lengths behind, and all pissed off.  Life is good!<P>-Kemp||||reg||6
