Z||000021||artherd||08-10-2001||05:15 AM||||heh, that's a pretty extreme spanking :)<P>I suppose that either the driver cannot drive, or that it was a DX coupe with a sticker :P) (did it have 15" alloy rims? <BR>the SIs have their own rims, although <BR>this is no certinty.)<P>As it's been said, it's a POS^H^H^H civic, of COURSE you spanked it :)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000022||chester||08-10-2001||08:35 AM||||Good kill. What makes it even better is THAT HE ASKED FOR IT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I haven't come across a Honda that gave me any grief yet.  There have been times where I would actually hit the brakes to let them catch up and pull away without effort. Yeah, you know, those tall spoiler, can't see the color of the paint thru all the stickers, loud pipe ones. Oh, and I have a friend that has a VTEC SI, I think its a 99 and yes, it has some balls but I was able to take him every time.  It was completely stock and I was running him with my stock 2.8 with 185,000 miles at the time.  We did this multiple times cause he couldn't belive that I was whooping him.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> He dosen't want to run me anymore now that I built the motor so I go after 5.0 Mudstains instead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||14
